@talks work:galley
// TW1, the Talk a while work pools: Galley (plans/work-pools-plan.html, decided 2026-10-20). Ids work.galley.<slug>;
// topic always "work". Brennan has her own talks and skips these. Bartenders: madsen-ivo, haddad-tamsin (leaves day
// 203); they skip the dinner-rush talk. Dlamini covers for Brennan Fri-Sat. Cadet: sorensen-agnes.
// Notgood (Walsh, Dlamini), exams (Haddad): no doubt or exam talk.

== rush
when: tier>=acquaintance !who:brennan|madsen-ivo
them: Dinner rush: seventy-five people in three hours. You stop being a person. You're hands.
them: Then it's over, you sit on an upturned crate, and it's the best seat on the ship.   #warm
ask: When in your day do you finally get to sit down?
listen: Do you ever get to eat hot?
  them: Never. Cold dinner, standing up, half eight. Wouldn't change it. Mostly.   #funny
share: After my shift. The first chair I find.
  them: The first chair's always the best one. That's science.   #funny
cheer: I don't. I just lean on things.
  them: Leaning's sitting for people with jobs. You'll do.   #funny

== onions
when: tier>=acquaintance !who:brennan|madsen-ivo
them: I chopped forty onions this morning. My eyes have given up crying. They've seen too much.
them: There's a count, you know. Who's chopped the most this season. It's very serious.   #funny
ask: Is there a bit of your job that's just repetition?
listen: Who's winning the onion count?
  them: Varga, by three. Dlamini says it's rigged. It's not. Varga's just fast.   #funny
share: Scrubbers. Same steps every time.
  them: Then you know. Same steps, every time, and one day you're fast without trying.
cheer: Walking to work. Very repetitive.
  them: Ha. The commute's the same here too. One lift.   #funny

== bar-stories
when: tier>=acquaintance who:madsen-ivo|haddad-tamsin
them: Behind the bar you hear everything. Not on purpose. People just tell a bartender.
them: I never repeat a word. That's the job. Pour the drink, keep the secret.   #warm
ask: Who do you tell things to, aboard?
listen: What's the oddest thing anyone's told you?
  them: Can't say. Bar rules. But it involved a cactus and a love of opera.   #funny
share: My bunkmates. And now you.
  them: Good. Everyone needs someone. I'm glad you've got a few.   #warm
cheer: The lift. It's a great listener.
  them: The lift's very discreet. Bartender-level discreet.   #funny

== six-trays
when: tier>=colleague who:madsen-ivo|walsh-esme|varga-tariq|dlamini-lukas
them: I can carry six trays at once. It took a year and a lot of broken cups.
them: Now I do it without thinking. Brennan says it's the only show-off she allows.   #funny
ask: What's a skill you've got that once seemed impossible?
listen: How many cups broke?
  them: Thirty-one. Brennan kept count. She keeps count of everything.   #funny
share: Stripping a scrubber in one go.
  them: Then you know the feeling. Impossible, then hard, then just Tuesday.
cheer: Eating while walking. Perfectly.
  them: A galley skill too. We could hire you.   #funny

== learned-by-ear
when: tier>=colleague !who:brennan|sorensen-agnes
them: Brennan cooks by ear. She taught me to listen to a pan. I thought she was joking.
them: Now I hear "done" from across the galley. It's a hiss that goes quiet. You'll laugh.   #funny
ask: Who taught you to do something by feel, not by the book?
listen: What does "nearly done" sound like?
  them: A bit busier. Like a crowd before the speech. Then it settles. Then it's done.
share: Someone at home. Fixing things by ear.
  them: Same school, different pan. Everyone good learns that way eventually.   #warm
cheer: Nobody. I use the timer.
  them: Brennan would take the timer off you. Gently. Then firmly.   #funny

== again
when: tier>=friend !who:brennan|walsh-esme|dlamini-lukas
them: My first month, I burnt a whole tray of the Sunday bread. Brennan's bread.
them: She didn't shout. She handed me the flour and said "Again." We were there till midnight.   #warm
ask: Who taught you the thing you're proudest of?
listen: What did she say after?
  them: Nothing. Next Sunday she let me take it out of the oven. That said everything.   #warm
share: Someone who stayed late to help me.
  them: Those are the ones you remember. Not the hard bit. The staying.   #warm
cheer: Nobody. I'm self-taught. Badly.
  them: Self-taught still counts. Brennan would say so too.   #warm

== feed-people
when: tier>=friend !who:brennan
them: Know what this job means to me? Every person on this ship eats today. Every single one.
them: Doesn't matter what kind of day they've had. There's a hot plate. That's us.   #warm
ask: What's the simplest good thing your work gives people?
listen: Does anyone ever skip dinner?
  them: Sometimes. Then there's a covered plate on the grab shelf with their name on it. Always.   #warm
share: Hot water. Nobody thinks about it.
  them: Then we're the same. Hot water, hot dinner. Nobody thinks. Everybody's glad.   #warm
cheer: Working lamps. Very bright work.
  them: Ha. Bright work. We'll put that on a sign.   #funny

== galley-habit
when: tier>=friend !who:brennan
them: The galley gave me a habit. I can't eat anywhere without checking how they cut the onions.
them: On leave at a café I sent a note to the kitchen. A nice one. They were confused.   #funny
ask: What does your job make you notice that nobody else would?
listen: What did the note say?
  them: "Lovely onions. Very even. Well done." I stand by it.   #funny
share: Every machine that's slightly off.
  them: Ha. Then we'd be awful together on leave. Noticing everything.   #funny
cheer: Which biscuit tin is fullest.
  them: That's not a job habit. That's survival. Respect.   #funny
